# Future work — surfaces/blocks

- Choosing a list depth while dragging. A dropped item keeps its own depth, clamped under
  the block above; the pointer's x does not choose a level. Rows and columns belong to the
  table surface.

- Drag-scroll at the viewport edges. A drag that reaches the top or bottom of the scroll area
  stops there. Alt+↑/↓ is the keyboard answer meanwhile.

- Touch on a real device. The path was probed only with synthetic touch pointer events plus a
  keyboard-driven selection. Long-press, a scroll fighting the capture, or stylus hover would
  only show up on hardware.
